# PURPOSE:
# This file contains shared environment variables for development and testing.
# It is maintained for developers, automated agents, and development workflows.
#
# ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION:
# - All configured values are strictly for non-production environments.
# - Production credentials and configuration must be managed separately.
# - Never use these values in production deployments.
#
# CONFIGURATION INTEGRITY:
# - Do not delete, clear, mask, or replace existing values with placeholders.
# - Do not regenerate or overwrite this file during routine development.
# - Preserve existing variables and values unless a change is authorised.
# - Add or update variables only when required by the application.
# - Shared development credentials may be rotated periodically.
#
# MAINTENANCE:
# - This policy header must remain intact and must not be removed.
# - Developers and AI agents must respect these rules during all changes.
# - Any credential rotation must be coordinated and documented.
#
# SECURITY:
# - Only approved, isolated development credentials may be stored here.
# - Never introduce production secrets or sensitive personal credentials.
# - Report suspected credential exposure instead of silently modifying values.
# =============================================================================

